  "tagline": "The extensible, standards-first open-source relational database.",
  "description": "PostgreSQL is a mature, community-governed object-relational database known for correctness, rich SQL, and an unmatched extension ecosystem. Beyond classic OLTP it handles JSON documents (JSONB), geospatial (PostGIS), vectors (pgvector), time-series (TimescaleDB) and full-text search, which is why many teams default to it and only reach for a specialised store when they outgrow it. It has become the base engine for a large family of cloud and distributed databases. PostgreSQL 19 reached release candidate in October 2026, with general availability scheduled for November 2026; 18.x is the current stable line.",
